rectangle "==Room Service\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nLets friends play one world together (server/): a Cloudflare Worker that makes rooms and a Durable Object per shared world that keeps the world and each player's progress, checks every message, and relays positions and edits between up to 100 players. The moderator can make a copy of a world to play as one of its players (server/src/copy.js), apart from the real one, download a whole world as a backup file and put a world that's gone back from one (server/src/backup.js), and has a page listing every world's players, sortable by progress (server/src/admin.js). It also keeps each player's own world for every device they link, by a secret sync key (server/src/vault.js, src/game/sync.js). See server/README.md for the rules and security limits." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0=>> as RoomService

rectangle "MORE THAN ENOUGH\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-TU9SRSBUSEFOIEVOT1VHSA==>> {
  rectangle "Web Application\n<size:16>[Container: HTML/CSS/JavaScript modules]</size>" <<Boundary-V2ViIEFwcGxpY2F0aW9u>> {
    rectangle "==AUTO\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nThe AUTO button (formerly Perfect): while held (and no sheet or dialog is up, and the player isn't steering, gathering or working a tile) it asks the brain for the next intent about four times a second and has the Controller carry it out, the same calls a tap makes. Keeps the badge (what it's doing), waits at Embark with a toast, and keeps the screen awake while held." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.AUTO
    rectangle "==Camera\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nMaps world (x, y, height) to screen pixels and back (project/unproject) with zoom and a fixed slight lean; picking hits the top or face you see. Also the visible tile range." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Camera
    rectangle "==Renderer\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nPaints all floor tiles before standing objects in north-to-south row order. Physical light shades each device-pixel-aligned terrain face in painter order. Static standing art shares an 8M-pixel/128-entry LRU of source-picture and 64 opacity buckets; animated and vector-only objects use a capacity-reused viewport-clipped transparent patch; no flat darkness mask slices raised art. Gameplay terrain stays live; the atlas owns distant map zoom. Local viewport-bounded masks preserve higher foreground terrain occlusion without clipping feet against equal-height floor. The faint visibility pass omits character and boat shadows; placement ghosts share the masks, Wiki focus and map mode retain their independent paths, and renderer fault recovery restores canvas clipping. The default player is Mica, a compact flat orange-hooded repairer with skinned split coat/patch, explicit-time mesh-eye blinks and curious idle/recovery poses, actual-cargo protective carrying and world inspection, with eight snapped world headings: twenty-one bone hierarchy with four weighted cloak panels, one-handed mining from the shaft's end and fixed-length arm IK to the WORK_HANDS targets in work-motion.js, earned palm-bound baskets and belt lanterns from work-equipment.js, free-hand assembly and a one-cycle coalescing actor queue with captured work facing, torso and head counterbalance, articulated elbows and wrists, and pure two-bone leg IK plus layered action curves from rig-motion.js. rig-model.js builds the rig without a renderer and names its solids and their joints and grips; rig-clips.js finds crossing triangles between them, which the unit sweep and the local dev build treat as a fault. rigged-character.js lazily bundles vendored Three.js and reuses one 320x448 WebGL surface composited into the 2D canvas. Wiki, a four-bone mycelium sprite with a skinned folding cap (wiki-model.js, pure pose in wiki-motion.js), rides the hood bone in the same pass and outline; src/game/wiki.js decides what it looks at and says (a long press on the map asks it), Mica and Wiki have no pointer hit targets; gestures pass to the world, and focus.js rings what it talks about in Wiki teal around the whole object. pickaxe-model.js supplies cached six-tier palm/back equipment and offline-baked matching icons, one flat fill mesh per tier with no ink shell; the character contour outlines it while equipped and a 2D silhouette stamp outlines the icons. Action/boat feedback shares canonical timing; presentation never runs simulation ticks. Mica is not drawn while the rig loads; without WebGL and for friends, the 2D wanderer stands in. A cached multisampled color target and one alpha-derived screen-space ink pass outline the complete figure, replacing per-piece hulls. Exact sRGB fills are preserved, with no CPU readback in normal rendering. Geometry, combined-pass draw calls and compressed module size are bounded. resource-models.js builds four canonical 3D materials and offline vector views through scripts/resource-art.mjs; icons/deposits/small piles remain cached texture-pack SVGs at runtime, flat value planes over one whole-object ink silhouette with no face or part edges. No player text." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Renderer
    rectangle "==Effects\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nParticles, floating text and flyers (resources homing into the pack), with budgets and a flyer lifetime so bursts stay cheap." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Effects
    rectangle "==HUD and Sheet\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nSemantic HUD groups share a bounded space policy: resources and horizontal navigation at the top, a fixed version slot below Settings, world status and metadata in one row, and fixed essential action slots. Optional detail collapses in order: performance, friend names, status, Messages. Viewport-defined communication and action regions keep Messages and preview anchors stable when panels open. A separate panel policy lets roomy desktop left logs coexist with right-side Equipment cards or menu sheets; compact screens share expanded disclosure space. Explicit Equipment disclosure opens a compact lights card with a separate crafting view; Settlement combines construction and current-layer site improvements through approach-before-action controller commands. Automatic compaction preserves message preferences and never reveals controls because of warnings. Whole-client fullscreen uses explicit gestures and actual browser state, handles prefixed APIs and unsupported/installed-view help, refreshes the viewport without locking orientation, and never changes game saves. Localized inspection, persistent per-world messages, earnings and the shared sheet remain integrated." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.HUDandSheet
    rectangle "==Audio\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nA small WebAudio synth unlocked by the first gesture: per-material gather voices, collect/build/upgrade/fanfare cues and an extractor hum. Takes parameters, never reads game state." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Audio
    rectangle "==Look\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nWhat everything looks like: the game's one pack (packs/default/). Loads and rasterises its pictures per size, picks variants and animation frames. An unavailable essential startup pack fails with picture/URL details. HTML pictures never emit empty URLs: missing IDs/slots keep labels/layout with a placeholder and a structured fault. Optional DOM resource errors remain nonfatal, with bounded pre-boot queuing and element/request/catalog/build/HTTP diagnostics carried into Problems with world context and map-tap breadcrumbs. Card picture-slot and actual Geode mouse-click tests guard the path. Drawing code and the HUD ask it for colours and pictures by thing id; players cannot load their own." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Look
    rectangle "==Yard\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nKeeps the stockpile's layout in step with the inventory (at most five times a second), tracks which tiles big piles cover, and makes changes visible like 2048: ten piles slide together into the bigger one they became, moved piles slide, new piles grow in, spent piles puff." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Yard
    rectangle "==Storage\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript + localStorage]</size>\n\nGuarded localStorage: load, save (reporting failures, never over another tab's save) and setting aside a save it can't read rather than writing over it, plus per-browser view settings. All solo collection models share normal saves, backup imports and per-seed archives. Earlier depot keys remain read-only recovery sources; incompatible local-collection worlds do not connect to rooms." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Storage
    rectangle "==Together\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript + WebSocket]</size>\n\nPlaying together (src/game/together.js): joins a shared world from a QR link (#join=room.invite) or opens a moderator's copy of one (#copy=room.key; src/game/copy.js keeps the browser's storage in memory then), relays your position, world edits and progress to the room and applies what it sends after checking it (src/net/protocol.js). Keeps friends and their states (online, away, connection lost, offline) for the renderer and the HUD chips, and makes the QR code for the sign your wanderer holds up in the world (src/vendor/qrcode.js). The worlds you've been in, their generated names and the Worlds screen that switches between them are in src/game/worlds.js; the friend chips and the Players screen (everyone in the world) are drawn by src/game/players.js." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Together
    rectangle "==Sync\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript + HTTPS]</size>\n\nYour own world on every device you link (src/game/sync.js): the device that shows the QR on the Another device screen (src/game/devices.js) makes a secret sync key, the one that opens its link (#link=key) takes it. Each keeps the world it plays in the room service's vault while it's played and takes the newest when it comes to the front; the world played last carries on, and only when both played the same world does the which-world question come up (src/game/fork.js). Brings a world back to a browser that forgot it." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Sync
    rectangle "==Main Loop\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nWires the modules together and owns the current state (game.state, replaced on embark/reset). Schedules the shared fixed-tick engine independently of drawing. Each simulation tick steers, steps the Core, reveals fog, works held input and ticks AUTO; presentation separately updates effects, save/HUD timers and rendering. A frame, a drawing layer or a tap that throws is skipped and kept as a problem report (faults.js, problems.js); only frames failing in a row stop the game. Exposes window.MTE_GAME for the browser tests." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.MainLoop
    rectangle "==Tick and Deadline Engine\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nShared 60 Hz logical clock. Browser catch-up is bounded; the headless runner coalesces stationary ticks ending at AUTO/goal deadlines, retaining fine motion and first Embark eligibility. Cumulative battery intervals preserve daylight transitions. Injected controller, AUTO and input interfaces keep scheduling independent of presentation. Blocked UI suspends AUTO-owned movement." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.TickandDeadlineEngine
    rectangle "==AUTO Developer Viewer\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nLazy single-player viewer booted before normal world loading. Lazily loads viewer-only styles and labels. Runs the shipped AUTO session in bounded real-time work slices at selectable speed, renders the normal client view, and retains separate IndexedDB worlds. The evaluation runner imports the same session." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.AUTODeveloperViewer
    rectangle "==Input\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nRaw touch/mouse/keyboard to intents: drag-anywhere joystick, tap, hold Gather (button or Space), hold AUTO (button or P), the Trail stroke (hold Gather and draw), pinch/wheel/button zoom, and sheet shortcuts. Holds no game state; calls the handlers it is given." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Input
    rectangle "==Controller\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nApplies intents to the game: tap (descend, harvest, collect, or walk there round obstacles: planWalk/walkAim in core paths.js, replanned when a hoped-open route through fog turns out blocked), Gather (collect, else harvest, else Explore walks to the nearest resource) and its hold, AUTO's intents (perform), Trail sweeps (every way of working a tile takes turns on one hand clock, core pace.js), going down and up between layers, buying, building, embarking, resetting. One queued approach/action routes observed cardinal contact sites once per order, faces the object, then calls the Core. New movement, orders or layer/world changes cancel it. Crafting and carried equipment need no destination. Each calls the Core, then triggers effects, sound, HUD and a save." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication.Controller
  }

  rectangle "==Pictures\n<size:16>[Container: JSON + SVG]</size>\n\nLanternlight (packs/default/): pack.json mapping every thing in the Catalog to its SVG pictures and colours. Required before the game draws anything; unit tests check it against the Catalog." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.Pictures
  rectangle "==Simulation Core\n<size:16>[Container: JavaScript modules (browser + Node)]</size>\n\nThe game rules (src/core/). Pure and deterministic: no DOM, no clock, no Math.random. Terrain is a pure function of (x, y, z, seed), state is a plain object, and the same modules run in the browser and in Node tests." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore
}

